Subject: [PATCH] Add AdvancedColumnFamilyOptions::blob_dir

Lets blob files be placed on a different volume than the SST files.

Stock RocksDB derives every blob file path from `cf_paths.front().path`, so
blob files always sit alongside the SST files of the first configured path.
`db_paths`/`cf_paths` therefore cannot tier large values: they distribute SST
files by level while every blob file stays put. This adds a per-column-family
`blob_dir` (empty = the historical `cf_paths.front()` behavior) and routes all
blob path derivation through a single `ImmutableCFOptions::GetBlobDir()`
accessor.

Sites updated: blob file creation and reads; directory fsync after flush and
compaction (a blob directory outside cf_paths has no handle in `Directories`,
so its entries were never synced — ColumnFamilyData now owns one); the
obsolete-blob-file path recorded for deletion; the CollectAllDBPaths scan; the
directory created at DB open; both DestroyDB overloads; Env path registration
via GetDbPaths; GetLiveFilesStorageInfo (checkpoint/backup); the column-family
metadata path; full-file checksum verification; the flush/compaction listener
info; and the direct-write blob partition manager, which otherwise writes to
`dbname_` regardless (only overridden when blob_dir is explicitly set, so the
default path is unchanged).

Because a blob file's directory is derived from the option rather than recorded
per file (unlike an SST's MANIFEST path index), the option is immutable and
changing it on a populated DB strands the existing blob files. RocksDB cannot
enforce that without persisting more state, so the constraint is documented
here and enforced by the consumer: @harperfast/rocksdb-js compares the request
against the blob_dir persisted in the OPTIONS file and refuses a mismatching
open. `blob_dir` is deliberately the LAST field of AdvancedColumnFamilyOptions
— inserting mid-struct would shift every following field's offset and silently
mismatch code compiled against stock headers.

`ROCKSDB_HAS_CF_BLOB_DIR` is defined in advanced_options.h so downstream code
can feature-detect and still compile against an unpatched RocksDB.

Rebase note: authored against v11.8.1 (the version pinned by rocksdb-js).
Re-check the blob path sites on every version bump — 11.8.1 added the
direct-write partition manager, which was a new one.

Downstream-only (HarperFast). Not submitted upstream.
