+  // NOTE: kept last on purpose. Inserting a field mid-struct changes the
+  // offsets of every field after it, so code compiled against stock RocksDB
+  // headers would silently mismatch this build.
+  // The directory blob files for this column family are written to and read
+  // from. When empty (the default), blob files live in `cf_paths.front().path`
+  // (falling back to `db_paths.front().path`, then the DB name), which is the
+  // historical behavior.
+  //
+  // Setting this decouples blob placement from SST placement: SST files are
+  // still distributed across `cf_paths` by level (see `GetPathId()`), while
+  // every blob file for this column family goes here. This makes it possible
+  // to keep the LSM tree on fast storage while large values live on cheaper,
+  // higher-capacity storage, or vice versa.
+  //
+  // Unlike `cf_paths`, a blob file's location is NOT recorded per file in the
+  // MANIFEST -- it is derived from this option every time a blob file is
+  // opened, deleted, or reported. Consequences:
+  //
+  // - This option is NOT dynamically changeable, and it must not be changed
+  //   while blob files exist. Doing so orphans the existing blob files and
+  //   reads of the values they hold will fail with a "No such file or
+  //   directory" IO error. To migrate, move the blob files to the new
+  //   directory while the DB is closed, then reopen with the new value. This
+  //   is the same class of hazard as changing `DBOptions::wal_dir`.
+  // - The directory must not be shared with another DB, for the same reason
+  //   `cf_paths` entries must not be: blob file numbers come from a per-DB
+  //   VersionSet, so two DBs sharing a directory mint colliding names and each
+  //   deletes the other's live files during obsolete-file scanning. Column
+  //   families of the SAME DB draw from one file-number space and may share.
+  //
+  // The directory is created at DB open if it does not already exist.
+  //
+  // Default: empty (use cf_paths.front().path)
+  std::string blob_dir = "";
 };
 
 }  // namespace ROCKSDB_NAMESPACE
